.TH CYAML_TYPE_STR 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cyaml_type_str \- return a string name for a node's type
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cyaml.h>

const char *cyaml_type_str(cyaml node);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Return a static string literal that names the type of node, for example
"CYAML_INTEGER".  The function returns "CYAML_UNKNOWN" for a type value
that it does not expect.  This function is useful for diagnostics and
for test output.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
A static null-terminated string.  The caller must not free it.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cyaml_type (3)
